  questionText: 'Which solution/stain will you use to detect the

    starch?'
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: A solution of iodine has an orange-brown colour. If it is added
    to a sample that contains starch, the colour of the sample changes to a deep
    blue showing the presence of starch in the sample.
  options:
  - 'Lactophenol cotton blue '
  - 'Safranin '
  - 'Acetocarmine '
  - 'lodine '
  correctOptionIndex: 3
